id: pm-slack-standup-kovw
title: "Cursor-complete standup reporting windows: build from a certified event boundary and retain the exact next boundary"
description: "Build a standup from a certified event boundary and retain the exact next boundary so crashes or late/backdated appends do not silently skip work between time windows. Overlap check (re-run 2026-10-27): pm history events / listMutationEvents supply cursor-resumable mutation facts; pm-observer (evidence budgets), pm-context (context-pack cursor), pm-slack (outbox resume cursors) use cursors for their own domains; this package's --since/--days/--compare date windows and snapshots select periodic views. No sibling or CLI command builds standup reporting from a retained event boundary, so this adapts the core mutation cursors to standup reporting without adding another event journal. Acceptance: (1) restart after rendering produces the same packet; (2) a late append appears once in a later admitted window; (3) missing history/cursor coverage marks the report incomplete rather than empty."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags: []
